window.docContents[58].resolve({"/Standards-Reference-___-PKC-beside-ISO-80000-1-and-the-VIM/Secondary-entries___-bounds-and-kind-edges/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Standards-Reference-___-PKC-beside-ISO-80000-1-and-the-VIM--Secondary-entries___-bounds-and-kind-edges":{"contents":"* This work* Dybkær (2009)* ISO 80000-1:2022* VIM 3 (JCGM 200:2012)* VIM 4 2CD* LowerBound* §12.16 (order)* —* —* —* UpperBound* §12.16 (order)* —* —* —* ProductKind* §13.3.5* 6.3 (product of two quantities)* 1.22 quantity equation* 1.30 quantity equation* QuotientKind* §13.3.5* 6.3 (quotient of two quantities)* 1.22 quantity equation* 1.30 quantity equation* ReciprocalKind* §13.3.5* 6.3 (quotient of two quantities)* 1.22 quantity equation* 1.30 quantity equation\n\n* Bounds have no counterpart. LowerBound and UpperBound are quantities of one kind\nin the role of an endpoint. Neither ISO 80000-1:2022 nor either VIM edition defines\na bound or an interval of quantity values as a term. They rest on the order that the\nordinal level provides.* Kind edges are declared, not derived from dimensions. ProductKind, QuotientKind\nand ReciprocalKind record that one kind is the product, quotient or reciprocal of\nothers, and require every kind involved to be ratio-scale (Dybkær §13.3.5). In the VIM\na quantity equation relates quantities, and the kind of a product follows from the\nequation and is checked by dimension. Here the product of two quantities exists only\nwhere an edge is declared, and the dimension is a consequence that certifies the edge\nwithout deciding it: two kinds of the same dimension, such as energy and moment of\nforce, remain distinct results. ISO 80000-1:2022 6.3 gives the product and the\nquotient of two quantities for any two quantities, with no such condition, and does\nnot treat the reciprocal separately.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Standards Reference — PKC beside ISO 80000-1 and the VIM","header":"34.8. Secondary entries: bounds and kind edges","id":"/Standards-Reference-___-PKC-beside-ISO-80000-1-and-the-VIM/Secondary-entries___-bounds-and-kind-edges/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Standards-Reference-___-PKC-beside-ISO-80000-1-and-the-VIM--Secondary-entries___-bounds-and-kind-edges"}});